/-!
# Chapter B: representations and failure of factorization

The shared module-theoretic vocabulary of Definitions B.1.1–B.1.3 and B.1.6
is re-exported from `Representation.BinaryOffender`. It uses actual binary
representations, fixed subspaces and elementary abelian subgroups. In particular,
`IsBestOffender` denotes membership in the source's `P(G,V)` and
`IsMinimalBestOffender` denotes membership in `P*(G,V)`.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, §B.1,
1 March 2004 manuscript, printed pp. 67–70.
-/
